1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,429
This country's lowest point is higher

2
00:00:02,429 --> 00:00:04,550
than Britain's highest mountain.

3
00:00:04,550 --> 00:00:06,329
And it's completely surrounded

4
00:00:06,329 --> 00:00:07,750
by another country.

5
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:08,872
This is Lesotho,

6
00:00:08,872 --> 00:00:12,250
a kingdom of mountains inside South Africa.

7
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:15,550
Watch what happens if the sea starts to rise.

8
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:16,731
At 1,000 metres,

9
00:00:16,731 --> 00:00:20,200
almost half of South Africa is underwater.

10
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:22,881
At 1,400, about four-fifths is gone,

11
00:00:22,881 --> 00:00:25,750
and Lesotho still hasn't got wet.

12
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:29,413
No country on Earth has a higher lowest point.

13
00:00:29,413 --> 00:00:32,300
And its peak tops 3,400 metres.

14
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:34,567
So why is it a separate country?

15
00:00:34,567 --> 00:00:36,763
In 1868, its king asked Britain

16
00:00:36,763 --> 00:00:39,300
for protection from the Boers.

17
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:42,219
That kept his mountain kingdom apart.

18
00:00:42,219 --> 00:00:44,586
In 1966 it became independent,

19
00:00:44,586 --> 00:00:46,900
surrounded on every side.

20
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:49,500
They call it the Kingdom in the Sky.

21
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:52,866
Would you live in a country with no lowlands at all?
